321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Cost Efficiency Through Smart Trade-offs)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We prioritize affordable, commodity hardware like Raspberry Pi 4, YD-LiDAR, and standard cameras rather than specialized robotics systems. To bridge the compute gap, we rely on optimized perception pipelines, classical lightweight algorithms, and selective cloud offloading during a short initial mapping phase. This hybrid approach lets the platform operate efficiently on low-cost onboard compute while still accessing advanced models and high-accuracy perception when the mission demands it.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Robustness Through Mathematical Safety)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Full Autonomy Through Hierarchical State Management)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We implement a two-tier coordination architecture where a high-level YASMIN state machine governs mission-level logic such as rack-to-rack transitions, scanning sequences, recovery triggers, and return-to-home procedures, and this state machine orchestrates a lower-level Nav2 behavior tree responsible for navigation execution. Nav2 provides modularity, built-in recovery behaviors, and parallel execution paths, but we extend it with custom modules including a safe distance-aware costmap layer for aisle-constrained movement and a DR-CLF-CBF controller that ensures provable safety even under perception uncertainty. This hierarchical design allows the platform to reason about task progression at the mission level while maintaining reliable and adaptive motion behavior at the navigation layer. By separating global decision-making from local control, the system becomes more interpretable, reusable, and easier to evolve than traditional monolithic robotics architectures, especially as new sensing modalities, behaviors, and mission types are introduced.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
