589 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The Solution: Custom Retraction Mechanism)
/E (The Solution: Custom Retraction Mechanism)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
590 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (We looked at the retraction mechanism found in standard measuring tapes, specifically a coil spring system, to automatically eliminate slack. Using an off-the-shelf coil spring was not feasible because the torque was too high. The resulting tension would have pulled too hard on the lightweight camera and connectors. Hence, we designed and 3D printed a separate housing that mimics the coil spring logic but utilizes rubber bands. This provides just enough low-level tension to coil the retracted wires into the housing without putting stress on the camera components.)
/E (We looked at the retraction mechanism found in standard measuring tapes, specifically a coil spring system, to automatically eliminate slack. Using an off-the-shelf coil spring was not feasible because the torque was too high. The resulting tension would have pulled too hard on the lightweight camera and connectors. Hence, we designed and 3D printed a separate housing that mimics the coil spring logic but utilizes rubber bands. This provides just enough low-level tension to coil the retracted wires into the housing without putting stress on the camera components.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
