710 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Different subsystems require multiple voltage rails: the motors operate at 12 V, the Raspberry Pi 4 requires 5 V at 3 A, the Pico 2 uses 5 V at 0.05 A, and various sensors run on 3.3 V or 5 V. Regulating the 22.2 V battery directly with linear regulators would be inefficient and generate excessive heat, so a high-power buck converter is used to supply the system.)
/E (Different subsystems require multiple voltage rails: the motors operate at 12 V, the Raspberry Pi 4 requires 5 V at 3 A, the Pico 2 uses 5 V at 0.05 A, and various sensors run on 3.3 V or 5 V. Regulating the 22.2 V battery directly with linear regulators would be inefficient and generate excessive heat, so a high-power buck converter is used to supply the system.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
