/T (Limitations)
/E (Limitations)
/Alt ()
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Cloud-Based Initialization: High-quality rack segmentation during startup depends on cloud inference; poor connectivity can reduce initial rack-pose accuracy.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Lighting Sensitivity in QR Detection: XZing can momentarily fail under glare, reflections, or sudden lighting changes, requiring brief re-scans.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Localization-Dependent Virtual Lane: Lane quality depends on early SLAM stability; weak loop closures may cause small stand-off inaccuracies.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Assumes Structured Aisles: Virtual-lane construction works best in regular warehouse layouts; irregular spaces reduce reliability.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Restricted Recovery in Tight Aisles: Nav2 recovery actions are limited in very narrow corridors and may occasionally require operator assistance.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Commercialisation Path)
/E (Commercialisation Path)
/Alt ()
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The platform can transition to a deployable product through ruggedised enclosures, WMS/ERP integration, and onboard health monitoring for motors, lift mechanisms, and sensors. Its low-cost architecture and modular design make large-scale manufacturing practical while keeping the price far below existing AMR scanning solutions.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Scalability)
/E (Scalability)
/Alt ()
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The system scales effectively across warehouses of different sizes because it requires no external infrastructure and builds all navigation corridors directly from its SLAM map. Its low-cost, modular hardware design and lightweight autonomy stack make it easy to replicate and deploy in new locations, while cloud-assisted initialization naturally handles larger environments without adding onboard compute load. This allows the solution to expand from small pilot deployments to full-facility coverage with minimal configuration effort.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Future Scope)
/E (Future Scope)
/Alt ()
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Future improvements include moving more perception models fully onboard to eliminate cloud dependency, deploying lighting-robust QR detection, expanding lane-generation beyond structured aisles, and introducing advanced recovery motions for tight or dynamic environments. These enhancements would strengthen autonomy, reduce edge-case failures, and enable operation in a broader range of warehouse types.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
